  "details": "Worlds:\n\nUdon Sword 3 - wrld_232a7b05-3300-49cb-a2ac-a5fd196550fb\n\nUdon Sword 2 - wrld_3c5ac438-ad0f-450a-a323-57a14569d63a\n\nUdon Sword 1 - wrld_5ee932de-bb76-4381-8143-c38a0a79b573\n\nHUD issue:\n\nWhen there is a HUD bound to your character (when joining the player roster), entering TPV makes the HUD unstable. This also occurs in all Udon Sword worlds.\n\nUX issue:\n\nSee: https://feedback.vrchat.com/third-person-view/p/1745-k-scroll-wheel-conflicts-with-tpv-camera-when-pickup-is-held\n\nWhen holding the staff (or any item, in any world, for that matter), the scroll wheel will bring the item closer or further away, instead of move the TPV camera. I believe there should be an advanced option or toggle for this. F5 can still be pressed just fine, but the scroll wheel conflicts when an item is held.\n\nProximity issues:\n\n-In Udon Sword 3, there is another instance where some proximity-based dialogue won't trigger unless in FPV, or really close up in TPV.\n\n-[Not shown in video] In all Udon Sword games, desktop players must be a mage/healer. In Udon Sword 1, targeting other players with a healing or cure spell will instead target yourself in TPV.",
